[{:db/id "q-124151/selection/6baf0b13908e86d0d3e98bd84d8227f6e81cf605751878da03b99cb684091034" :answer/id #uuid "fc607ca2-dc0f-5dcf-b5ab-8787b5957366" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/37ba7b2e9b6f84d4a928cb18c5fb9c7a2cbaf6a564cc17b0c9cf8656e6970bf7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151/selection/88178ffc9a507445c68f4bf883d48e71966b01e27c5744f7ee86a2d4f24e7eb0" :answer/id #uuid "4636a2c5-65af-517e-8bbb-8c496042c988" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/38a060b98b529dbf687f9aab45d94545e7d83533fe73027b543cb7a88d914d72.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151/selection/4da559654895ee200adec5e6eb4371467cd4c411fd3ef467ae73eac42d8dc58b" :answer/id #uuid "5da552ab-a79e-5d43-b820-3d694d9216ed" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4bea3edd3fcde575e68e36e08fc4186863b12450802eb0ee37c841975983486.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151/selection/9cc2813448e72249b555c1b7c4c2f2c4829cad797c1b89dad595b731c3d74fca" :answer/id #uuid "8e01eb11-1d6a-5f16-9c9d-9f2c50bc4e41" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/ac6a03b4ef408f0f8b5cd6945ffa606eb948962330e5efd9005ff9fe199ad465.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151/selection/4bfb381025f0aaeca7e61d30fecc2d803d7e077a671d88425a234b8ec53db562" :answer/id #uuid "abb1674c-4043-55e6-8582-54c68730b08a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/ca23324a1f9e69156fd2752d599ef4d1331dd61ec81f61a44434f778b918fd1d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60697f37-5d57-5a84-90e2-a9271deeb18c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124151/selection/4da559654895ee200adec5e6eb4371467cd4c411fd3ef467ae73eac42d8dc58b" :answer-field/choices ["q-124151/selection/6baf0b13908e86d0d3e98bd84d8227f6e81cf605751878da03b99cb684091034" "q-124151/selection/88178ffc9a507445c68f4bf883d48e71966b01e27c5744f7ee86a2d4f24e7eb0" "q-124151/selection/4da559654895ee200adec5e6eb4371467cd4c411fd3ef467ae73eac42d8dc58b" "q-124151/selection/9cc2813448e72249b555c1b7c4c2f2c4829cad797c1b89dad595b731c3d74fca" "q-124151/selection/4bfb381025f0aaeca7e61d30fecc2d803d7e077a671d88425a234b8ec53db562"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124151" :question/id #uuid "3187ec42-ba90-5620-adf4-a7bfe030aeac" :question/math-academy-id "q-124151" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/33f7326ffe8318fca915e8cc7e02a2a4c280dd9377066f1870f3bb8067b22eb0.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u+3v+2,\\,y=v-2u.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+3v+2 \\\\ v-2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,2u+3v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-5,3)$ and $(10,0).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4bea3edd3fcde575e68e36e08fc4186863b12450802eb0ee37c841975983486.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124151/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ba09dd1-d219-5df2-adfa-d88d7b9fc481"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection/13911d5561191f775a13d70c9c14ccfbfe7a8fb6ed066f50a5174fec9e6bee5b" :answer/id #uuid "e114d5e1-02cd-5e0f-bbe4-ee9d8c970621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection/4e183f6269d3718bcde5d88bd80fd5be3aceace38306ffbf18f9c994edb8417e" :answer/id #uuid "7b0415c5-6bb9-538f-ae13-34f82602512e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,-17)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection/3fab62946530d24dfb6944e62006b21ccc89ab8d5c04c8c5946c3a5698064204" :answer/id #uuid "47cb455f-bcc9-5317-b539-73b025c14d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,23)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection/69b0f13a185765faa39442bbd0a8c4518011394b374f5571b4e89e387bfe720a" :answer/id #uuid "1ffca506-0257-577d-9e34-92afeede77ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(11,17)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection/a2a7ae47a0dfdc2772ffd06f0fbda3e7aeba6911dca3104b257ed34045b09bb9" :answer/id #uuid "9afbcb0d-033c-5906-9a0c-0c5eb7d3e7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(11,-23)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d167c20-f2e1-5a5a-9703-8fd24bcb86bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124156/selection/4e183f6269d3718bcde5d88bd80fd5be3aceace38306ffbf18f9c994edb8417e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124156/selection/13911d5561191f775a13d70c9c14ccfbfe7a8fb6ed066f50a5174fec9e6bee5b" "q-124156/selection/4e183f6269d3718bcde5d88bd80fd5be3aceace38306ffbf18f9c994edb8417e" "q-124156/selection/3fab62946530d24dfb6944e62006b21ccc89ab8d5c04c8c5946c3a5698064204" "q-124156/selection/69b0f13a185765faa39442bbd0a8c4518011394b374f5571b4e89e387bfe720a" "q-124156/selection/a2a7ae47a0dfdc2772ffd06f0fbda3e7aeba6911dca3104b257ed34045b09bb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124156" :question/id #uuid "8c9bb0aa-5707-5319-bed1-7d20e29a615c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124156" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=3v+u,\\,y=u-6v+3.\n$$\n\nLet $P(-2,3)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3v+u \\\\ u-6v+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v \\\\ u-6v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(7,-17).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124156/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ba09dd1-d219-5df2-adfa-d88d7b9fc481"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124156"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124178/selection/c1ebd4f7d7d6e12ed797853e7c4209b01f93944714b48cd2a2303b32c07ee133" :answer/id #uuid "c9387147-3c52-590d-ae19-083d431ffa62" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/947907e5a3581626420616f119cc126c08718a7d4c9323032fa3e1774dcc9537.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124178/selection/fca5b1fd774956976