/fca5b1fd774956976f57d0bf44aacae67b683a96bccb415cd505b636645b3be2" "q-124178/selection/fd3074f96772be026999288cff65a347902f16a526072ecc241b1f8e28a0683f" "q-124178/selection/2014762c0967c6c4f4d92bc97efacec97cea80906cec87ad6d58004e6b31a35e" "q-124178/selection/f8148c56444bcb4235eaa8546ad0d982970502495023b610863914ef283ef044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124178" :question/id #uuid "e5578bdc-3ff0-534a-8da8-40c48db3f6bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-124178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/afc9e81f3294803794ba0d62773958913cf7475a0718e77052212a149050aecf.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u+2v-2,\\,y=v-u+2.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+2v-2 \\\\ v-u+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+2v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-6,2)$ and $(8,1).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/8e57b4d47ef3c6ad1b1d70a97126aa865c4481ee67e16eaf4e79c09e3146b30d.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ba09dd1-d219-5df2-adfa-d88d7b9fc481"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection/662c277f350ac1a8ffcfa5efcf73a8a540e2cf3e387c66c7db66386198588dd2" :answer/id #uuid "1693998f-ab45-5bec-a343-cc5d77a5ad9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection/a6c55c00f7680bdaee7b804cc72ebddb62c1ff2e7a75036caf750160487e7ee9" :answer/id #uuid "a09dca29-a5e4-5ae7-803d-4417beab6aa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection/b2afa54a305d356589964276c742c30b434d533408abd40d6d86db616b984ffe" :answer/id #uuid "84354f8c-7b1e-581b-9d72-d44901b4a6ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection/e5c1f515261f1785c4411bf39e18fd362d120089b2df8fd0f85e3f972f37bf07" :answer/id #uuid "97b03400-a304-590f-8bf4-358a28ece2f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection/7898b015caa2a5b24b4c9e43acbaaa371c0f47a12e1365574e1322d58326243b" :answer/id #uuid "510b68a7-d999-56c8-8bf9-ccdea66bbc9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c3c23de-5cfc-57e5-a014-ffb79ba7607c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124144/selection/a6c55c00f7680bdaee7b804cc72ebddb62c1ff2e7a75036caf750160487e7ee9" :answer-field/choices ["q-124144/selection/662c277f350ac1a8ffcfa5efcf73a8a540e2cf3e387c66c7db66386198588dd2" "q-124144/selection/a6c55c00f7680bdaee7b804cc72ebddb62c1ff2e7a75036caf750160487e7ee9" "q-124144/selection/b2afa54a305d356589964276c742c30b434d533408abd40d6d86db616b984ffe" "q-124144/selection/e5c1f515261f1785c4411bf39e18fd362d120089b2df8fd0f85e3f972f37bf07" "q-124144/selection/7898b015caa2a5b24b4c9e43acbaaa371c0f47a12e1365574e1322d58326243b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124144" :question/id #uuid "c30de37e-94eb-5824-8c19-5f0e87550d0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124144" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-v+u+2,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(4,1)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-v+u+2 \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(5,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124144/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ba09dd1-d219-5df2-adfa-d88d7b9fc481"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124101"] :question/problem "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=3u+v-2,\\,y=u-2v+1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(3,2)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+v-2 \\\\ u-2v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(9,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection/3a136194ae1b4895c79f4141b817f00af945a7db314a445e7b150a7f4ff89172" :answer/id #uuid "249b0f6b-141a-5cb7-8b72-29e378c316d1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/d1e93d9ce18d7c75ab6432d53ae9ff72fd3fe2c89125a12dcd2d41a13100465d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection/909d301862b5ecb982005a80db3a1e172d368cbfd9eed951c45166d355abee76" :answer/id #uuid "ecb360b5-b763-50be-b8c6-005b54badfad" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/8254c51a8f1c9f0ca48f169fb48a938b07e5812b5be866d9ab25e5fbdffed368.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection/fe8486a4eb7b40d85cc55f8f5ae835c4d004cab6beac657d394bf127eea230df" :answer/id #uuid "07a9c971-297c-5726-8ca1-44528cca84fa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/6be30b91e0526e28530b4c5cfff6c0c5e7be53a77e587c5eb37a845b6cc0a189.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection/8f16f60a0fc1e844f0bc3c613a23d649976b7f3419238430d5da5546dc1d6d8a" :answer/id #uuid "86a6ea4a-8eac-5dc8-9b6e-f23513859643" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/27dbdbec3125bdef5109bf6aa549c9bcfe83175b42e660cc44977540de0ad112.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection/04fb9697d6bbdb3fd6879aa68a3765702bf5f3534a813e54e0a3cb2ebd707cbc" :answer/id #uuid "e267c004-9028-5c19-906a-9ac7373650af" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a7b171394aeccd9b807fc29ecf7c33f745c58bce3ed01bcf879a79d2edf97319.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15f0ea00-384c-5972-89b7-187fe7861818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124561/selection/3a136194ae1b4895c79f4141b817f00af945a7db314a445e7b150a7f4ff89172" :answer-field/choices ["q-124561/selection/3a136194ae1b4895c79f4141b817f00af945a7db314a445e7b150a7f4ff89172" "q-124561/selection/909d301862b5ecb982005a80db3a1e172d368cbfd9eed951c45166d355abee76" "q-124561/selection/fe8486a4eb7b40d85cc55f8f5ae835c4d004cab6beac657d394bf127eea230df" "q-124561/selection/8f16f60a0fc1e844f0bc3c613a23d649976b7f3419238430d5da5546dc1d6d8a" "q-124561/selection/04fb9697d6bbdb3fd6879aa68a3765702bf5f3534a813e54e0a3cb2ebd707cbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124561" :question/id #uuid "3d0ee1e3-75ae-50a8-b3f0-30dae7eb2a64" :question/math-academy-id "q-124561" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/79b09bcf02998adf6d7bf19e7d59cabdc563ff26266966440bbb49be53029ac3.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-\\frac{u+1}{2}\\le v\\le u+1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/539c74bf4d397916fd7ac11089fa9500bd71cdf2278891136785d6e792431b05.png)\n\n             \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-1,-1),(1,-1),$ and $(-2,2).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/adfe476bd2ca719996d612855ca5368bdea09370b7befcffb08a062db8587cbb.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fd0b67f-681b-5b1d-8be9-2ab2d1ca5e66"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124103"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a4a1d43bc68a44db24d22767630573ebd9aafb646196e212640c24f2650e7b17.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1-u}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/0d736c2e3fa2c4ba1872b045b8bdcf4def98a24337683e368bec337b810b6acb.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(0,-1),(1,0),$ and $(-2,0).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/1aed421f9d6458fb8b72a44c83703b3f1c0475cee9ef9ec2f0a4cfcaad74d7fc.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=3>0,$ this transformation preserves orientation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection/a931c259022775ddbfd2ade5c25a114a977f0ebed159b7096abb92fc894070cd" :answer/id #uuid "26141053-578a-52c3-8368-2f413e408a03" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4ab9f75402ccf20fa66cd08f910d8afed0314e063b835f4697450e595fbc3fe.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection/3ddbbaaca5d22e6ad178c43b2fa2f8af329f7a96e055c33cf73a40b69d8f5c65" :answer/id #uuid "59996a8b-ffe5-5f32-a0dc-7e768ed917b7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/c1219b3ee5d914ab1f202d337fe16ef1dc19ac654ddf8e214b01b9d58fb3633d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection/cf41178ce95933fd0ea4a41504945d5215ba5a42005a5ada5edc26840760c2c7" :answer/id #uuid "bf38ac1e-6796-5b44-9b06-497c143bb515" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/b64b00b28b3525b788e85a64f75ab5c7a163e40c28328d3386d416d9a0021800.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection/3751b22002ef90087898b8850fc8cf51071c7200c3fcb45e9c6deb5942375fbf" :answer/id #uuid "5f845cf8-07d2-5bb1-8e48-6c14a3a965d0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/509af7e65cf004433f66b89ccf93cce5897956e1b81a90a77a856f7c827450ba.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection/990ccee0013b4fa294a603fe40ddcf42f3445eed73b7a88dbd5c1f65151f3699" :answer/id #uuid "e4bb5947-545b-5128-beeb-3dc68ebba3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a3c550025c6f5e7d5227f3ec1ce3ddf9a5efb20531217fdcb9bed5605e7c36e3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e588d2ce-08e1-5b7c-a922-768c9cf803a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124650/selection/cf41178ce95933fd0ea4a41504945d5215ba5a42005a5ada5edc26840760c2c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-124650/selection/a931c259022775ddbfd2ade5c25a114a977f0ebed159b7096abb92fc894070cd" "q-124650/selection/3ddbbaaca5d22e6ad178c43b2fa2f8af329f7a96e055c33cf73a40b69d8f5c65" "q-124650/selection/cf41178ce95933fd0ea4a41504945d5215ba5a42005a5ada5edc26840760c2c7" "q-124650/selection/3751b22002ef90087898b8850fc8cf51071c7200c3fcb45e9c6deb5942375fbf" "q-124650/selection/990ccee0013b4fa294a603fe40ddcf42f3445eed73b7a88dbd5c1f65151f3699"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124650" :question/id #uuid "0b0635f9-acd6-5529-ae03-8909e67e025f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124650" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/d947e13c2b18ce786f03636d174604dd60e715ed0ce1929ff4ac98cf91084a50.png)\n\nConsider the rectangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=3u+2v-2,\\,y=2u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+2v-2 \\\\ 2u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/d0103ef8cdf76a3f80bd9be6314c2a693cbf9e51fe66f95228ccce1703f6775f.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-2,-1),(1,1),(3,2),$ and $(0,0).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/0b22301fac2a0d97c0f0d99b3c4d162e8965f5570522754a3e21fa124194f1c0.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fd0b67f-681b-5b1d-8be9-2ab2d1ca5e66"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection/f0dfda2eac87a6ce34b4dc3a74c625f15a83c303ed887dbee5aa830de424f453" :answer/id #uuid "5d64f1a2-3e15-5e33-9d8e-f0419023a53e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a1c56986c6de278a24b0d83d69b26822b4330d815b8f501db7da8f3d10e625da.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection/873f025f2ebb7722d3fdd2514a57afb4d7fead19f14cbb7e8b6c953ad616d0b2" :answer/id #uuid "10a35c72-c612-5acd-b619-867039402deb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/f17eeed2b5ab0b065ab0c4c7c7c669108ce4f0d8de8f69979316d12c2885d73e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection/c3a6abd8e7b6586f00de22b85f69a15b7d803edba4d80cb1adb170ef906aa00c" :answer/id #uuid "bc29d121-359c-513c-920a-c558b889ac47" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/01a8419fe9a435734f69c1913764423739b881fd6aa377a08f085e2ea7aab10b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection/14de1dcbf6076f84c868ca9c4b02e0682649ab48b587c69c59a891acd3feff4f" :answer/id #uuid "803efcb7-e723-5486-8fb5-1981680106bf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/9ebbc28d7bf9b1ec3e5adb15a036570f1a7025d0dcedab7f61610c09b0c4c423.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection/8fc90e30ff62b65a299b5ca50a352f6a86001ca98883f950ee984b3d8ee4f892" :answer/id #uuid "f261f6b9-24b2-5b20-b9ad-d372f6348573" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e181f53d2f99a2374739769ea5e5837de0acf8526717f0607e0e81dba4da0c1e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26ac11aa-8ae5-5483-8191-35b466449001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124569/selection/8fc90e30ff62b65a299b5ca50a352f6a86001ca98883f950ee984b3d8ee4f892" :answer-field/choices ["q-124569/selection/f0dfda2eac87a6ce34b4dc3a74c625f15a83c303ed887dbee5aa830de424f453" "q-124569/selection/873f025f2ebb7722d3fdd2514a57afb4d7fead19f14cbb7e8b6c953ad616d0b2" "q-124569/selection/c3a6abd8e7b6586f00de22b85f69a15b7d803edba4d80cb1adb170ef906aa00c" "q-124569/selection/14de1dcbf6076f84c868ca9c4b02e0682649ab48b587c69c59a891acd3feff4f" "q-124569/selection/8fc90e30ff62b65a299b5ca50a352f6a86001ca98883f950ee984b3d8ee4f892"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124569" :question/id #uuid "e48d3f9e-79f6-5f88-9764-fe40dc9cde3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124569" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/deff964a1833339681fc38b30e32ebd3081e7ba1c4b5aabd0f4998f60a2aa78c.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le v\\le 1,\\,\\frac{v-1}{2}\\le u\\le \\frac{1-v}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/daefc9e14775a955e5210f965e474c06bc7cac1df9306941b73190cc8bf62219.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-3,-2),(-1,2),$ and $(0,2).$ \n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/94a2a90dae43d1edb1f0154a8c7ac60b8c35352fd72d5193014b9bba204d192f.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124569/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fd0b67f-681b-5b1d-8be9-2ab2d1ca5e66"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124569"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection/8c55a19e18a56b5d6719fc26c15e663a5029b0c4c7fb6fa93cbbbfa6d56c9943" :answer/id #uuid "c9b2c15b-9e84-5c55-a1f0-7047412da540" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/bd95a6f92fc74e2f3b915de3b6ccda921b1f260ee6080f12a8ca54de243dae1c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection/6189e14025c0e8e295b11994aa969b52388331a01197b3c5ae08f6a94ec8ca25" :answer/id #uuid "d6d7ec30-ce77-5207-aaa2-8b5ba75115f5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/bbddd646e109123853cb4b00898f8042dd9fbb2225e2dd582920035e23e552ac.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection/c7353c4e7fdf9e7748e9ec334d236e8a037eb2ce9300b632a16d8c7282a2a7ab" :answer/id #uuid "f3a463f9-7459-5254-8fc7-a77d439630be" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/3131825a9fd81b0099f9049961c846d2383dcbb3effa5280bdc3818536104746.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection/a272d6bd99f03693115e2e9dae734d214bbae2c50109622ecf2edc399b5459a6" :answer/id #uuid "6e22dc28-3124-56e8-870c-91e5279fd375" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4c3f4e9d984fb71b0f5d34473cca7a825224d4a9db0c4ea18a4e232185b2f48.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection/e9a56bd4f7353ba4ca9ebeb69282128b97440951e2e1c9a0a362a6fe02e5571e" :answer/id #uuid "a5612992-a821-5d16-b253-f6a811fa8137" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/60f1c0c294345639995de964b397ee2e31365c35668a24a3a20ad87cdf7d8e6b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eefff25a-1262-54f4-aba3-375b8c9c00c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124571/selection/6189e14025c0e8e295b11994aa969b52388331a01197b3c5ae08f6a94ec8ca25" :answer-field/choices ["q-124571/selection/8c55a19e18a56b5d6719fc26c15e663a5029b0c4c7fb6fa93cbbbfa6d56c9943" "q-124571/selection/6189e14025c0e8e295b11994aa969b52388331a01197b3c5ae08f6a94ec8ca25" "q-124571/selection/c7353c4e7fdf9e7748e9ec334d236e8a037eb2ce9300b632a16d8c7282a2a7ab" "q-124571/selection/a272d6bd99f03693115e2e9dae734d214bbae2c50109622ecf2edc399b5459a6" "q-124571/selection/e9a56bd4f7353ba4ca9ebeb69282128b97440951e2e1c9a0a362a6fe02e5571e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124571" :question/id #uuid "c7eb367f-3cc1-5728-9bfc-7b0c473f7380" :question/math-academy-id "q-124571" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/9bfb4e21205db9550d88222e04449b9858137550b957ba652b3e6998dce8025c.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le u\\le \\frac{1-v}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/194428bede19351ba77866a9ca49f76b38c4327fd0a5e2c219afff9c14b12c28.png)\n\n             \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-2,0),(-1,-1),$ and $(0,2).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/02ab748669496bf50a8809cf822a969d731a18283d52272175fd5b615ef5b765.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=2>0,$ this transformation preserves orientation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fd0b67f-681b-5b1d-8be9-2ab2d1ca5e66"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "71ec5ded-460c-5c66-8ed0-87fcd3c087e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5a1be5d3-bc33-5f8c-913f-2c87703fa2c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5fac8f54-711e-5e1c-ac70-e382b4642d76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "63c535af-7cd8-5614-a0e9-9b6fbd753626" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d3be1eae-2cd4-56b5-801c-f6fe5e399b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "774cccfc-2e55-57ca-abe5-29c616377f1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124192/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-124192/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-124192/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-124192/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-124192/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-124192/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124192" :question/id #uuid "06e1c006-ef77-5600-9c9c-1814cfed601d" :question/math-academy-id "q-124192" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v+u+1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-3$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v+u+1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124192/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6b6f32d9-7dc2-5632-8c33-2ba6c723a826" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "34b3eae8-e1ba-5d0f-8953-964f56790324" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5517f850-817c-51da-ab3b-1b3ab1932029" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7d17008d-7b95-52ce-96a6-1ee7eec3dec0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f4af82fd-60a1-5080-9fd9-aaaa46a92477" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a799794b-0005-5d4d-bc0e-e6ffba540047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124330/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-124330/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-124330/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-124330/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-124330/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-124330/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124330" :question/id #uuid "b984558d-7a5b-5815-b421-f9aecb0d672a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124330" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-2v+1,\\,y=4u-v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-4$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v+1 \\\\ 4u-v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=0\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-2)=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124330/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "265654b9-33a4-59a1-bc49-6f43a3af9c80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b02df7f6-72aa-5b29-a8c7-e7f68876b230" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e5359659-7028-57fd-948a-564059763874" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "133afa23-fbbc-530a-85ee-d10e18393d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c5080850-0f92-5e66-bf9e-eba895f1b27f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2426634-cac1-5dbc-9533-c56bee455598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124322/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-124322/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-124322/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-124322/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-124322/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-124322/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124322" :question/id #uuid "e5f774fd-e4fc-5b69-88ef-de7d2e0c0984" :question/math-academy-id "q-124322" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+3v-5,\\,y=2v+u-4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=1$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v-5 \\\\ 2v+u-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124322/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6b30bc55-23cc-55fc-9dd0-cddc9c5c21a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ad1129c4-72b7-5438-b8e7-1f51ed3e3cae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "47f5ccc5-b42c-5a9c-977e-1fc2cb0bcb2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "cb255f2d-8b96-5eba-99d4-50f741b46662" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "232d98ed-de96-5d52-bb98-d90b111905f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d30971d4-a8c1-5ace-802b-cb915616c692" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124326/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-124326/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-124326/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-124326/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-124326/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-124326/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124326" :question/id #uuid "f53de4b4-b46c-561f-a45d-98fcac1e0352" :question/math-academy-id "q-124326" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-1$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124326/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124326"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "30ca0044-eff4-59a2-b47c-df7db644207c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f1d78a18-a389-5c36-b436-1dadfcf62895" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "eaff95e0-9b6a-5d9c-9960-7fafe1c1549b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f07a2c21-7e37-5c7d-b279-2521f17c5c51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer/id #uuid "b3d4d8fb-1295-5c6c-90c9-7aac404ae356" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7138500b-3e5e-533c-93d2-4d4c2e868a98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124327/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer-field/choices ["q-124327/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-124327/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-124327/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-124327/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-124327/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124327" :question/id #uuid "2e401db1-cd05-5461-a2d6-1762b7bf5609" :question/math-academy-id "q-124327" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-2u,\\,y=u+3v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-7$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-2u \\\\ u+3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=(-2)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1=-7.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124327/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162141"] :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-u \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-2|=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e1816eaa-8b90-5fc4-ae31-d151ee3371af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "83c07426-e5d6-5767-8cfa-8d3b1a09289e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "10c14f76-8538-5f3b-b8ce-9ff717578ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3f85d7c9-b0b9-5925-a556-1006b895d34e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "81cec101-c83f-59b7-a418-447a48b65d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c09fbbc6-2fed-51fb-af7a-34feab6b1522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162178/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-162178/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-162178/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-162178/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-162178/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162178/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162178" :question/id #uuid "ff565126-48c4-516c-aa72-0e5197334a19" :question/math-academy-id "q-162178" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-4|=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c087f5ef-10c1-5e5c-9008-9342823454aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "71ef0b74-d165-5447-a54c-5e6b65d474ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "85f67222-98d9-5b50-aaf7-c872c258c085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "049e936f-4f8f-5171-b709-313de6963d50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d62e3233-0844-5758-abb2-e8eade0dcfad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cec7d97-c8e5-5fb8-9720-b0cfa060960f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162195/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-162195/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-162195/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162195/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-162195/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-162195/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162195" :question/id #uuid "52780571-6d1c-586f-ab0a-dbad6ab068ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-162195" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-2v-3,\\,y=u-v+2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-2v-3 \\\\ u-v+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|0|=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162195/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162195"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "49872bab-dc84-5549-9471-9c4d14960ab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "91384bfb-cb37-5ae4-8c17-00a129eac8e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "681a1c14-2ecf-5c8b-aac3-5fc5fafe2c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "86a290e0-0986-5e12-aa7d-6551d43fec5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a6902d19-6d06-596c-a291-42ce8e581141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "36b9b027-f3f5-515d-bfbb-cad289c94da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162182/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-162182/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-162182/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-162182/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162182/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-162182/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162182" :question/id #uuid "5b371d41-ceca-56dc-ac18-9bd2edcd18b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162182" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-2)=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-1|=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162182/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162182"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "662701fc-446c-569c-8817-4f15ab51d735" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "7d8349db-d2bb-5f93-80a1-d479ceb0dab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "932fbc85-6f2e-5834-9234-7f7757fb98bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d9084e0a-b214-582c-b727-c03c4e4f2f3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a514b866-6d7b-51b3-abb0-24357f396e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbf72d4-ff11-5a9e-b815-b69cbe2d55d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162193/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-162193/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-162193/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-162193/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-162193/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-162193/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162193" :question/id #uuid "5086ef87-75ae-5d31-a148-7c6005c17c39" :question/math-academy-id "q-162193" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+5v+2,\\,y=1-u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+5v+2 \\\\ 1-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+5v \\\\ -u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 5=5.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|5|=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162193/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162193"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12425"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/2abec0420bf322120bb37135af682a7bc04c97c86d7bf1bdfd04012a8355883c.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overline{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $\\mathbf T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx = u - v + 7, \\qquad y = u + v +1.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overline{PQ}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ is the segment $\\overline{P'Q'}$ in the $xy$-plane. Find $\\overline{P'Q'}.$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v+7 \\\\ u+v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $\\mathbf T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overline{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overline{P'Q'}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overline{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $\\mathbf b$ in each column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\mathbf u$ under $\\mathbf T$ is given by $A\\mathbf u + \\mathbf b.$ So, by applying $\\mathbf T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(0,-2)$ and $(-3,1).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/61508357c514f50b27498bee50dce36d22b7f55f0baf8c2d6a58ad2d53dc879d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12426"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/dd8b1407add93e72afccf2138cc818df63d47fdaa6ccc23e843a5602d8c1dbd8.png)\n\n          \n\nConsider the rectangle $\\Delta$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta  = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: -1\\leq v \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $\\mathbf T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx = u - v + 1, \\qquad y = u+v\n$$\n\nFind the image of $\\Delta$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $\\mathbf T.$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v+1 \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $\\mathbf T$ maps the boundary of $\\Delta$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $\\Delta,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/69d92e24d5b0c81e54d3878793efe7c07d16fc963222997fe4fec4ffb3f93bd5.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $\\mathbf b$ in each column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\mathbf u$ under $T$ is given by $A\\mathbf u + \\mathbf b.$ So, by applying $\\mathbf T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(1,-2), (3,0), (1,2),$ and $(-1,0).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/ddd14bdebe21c830396e044721811cf6b9c7bd7db067e4d0ff7d35e02a592894.png)\n\n          \n\nNotice that since $\\det(A) = 2 >    0,$ this transformation is orientation-preserving." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12427"] :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $\\mathbf T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx = v - u-6, \\qquad y = v -2u  .\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $\\mathbf T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $\\det(A) = 1$\n\n- The transformation $\\mathbf T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-u-6 \\\\ v-2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $\\mathbf T$ is $[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $\\det(A) > 0,$ the affine transformation $\\mathbf T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12436"] :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $\\mathbf T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx = 3u+4, \\qquad y = 4v - 2u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+4 \\\\ 4v-2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u \\\\ -2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $\\mathbf T$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|\\det(A)| = |12| =12.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
